  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ザラツキエノコログサ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B6%E3%83%A9%E3%83%84%E3%82%AD%E3%82%A8%E3%83%8E%E3%82%B3%E3%83%AD%E3%82%B0%E3%82%B5",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106363006,
      "text": "ザラツキエノコログサ Setaria verticillata (L.) はイネ科の植物の1つ。エノコログサによく似ているが、穂から突き出す刺毛が強くざらつくことで区別される。穂が互いに引っかかり合って絡まっていることがよくある。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Setaria verticillata」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Setaria_verticillata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1335317530,
      "text": "Setaria verticillata is a species of grass known by the common names hooked bristlegrass, rough bristle-grass and bristly foxtail. It is native to Europe, but it is known on most continents as an introduced species and often a noxious weed. It is a hardy bunchgrass which grows in many types of urban, cultivated, and disturbed habitat. It is a weed of many types of agricultural crops, growing in vineyards and fields. Herbicide-resistant strains have been noted."
    }
  },
